  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sheikh Abrar Sheikh Gaffar vs The State Of Maharashtra on 27 May, 2022 Bench: D.Y. Chandrachud, Bela M. Trivedi 1 In The Supreme Court Of India Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Criminal Appeal No 880 of 2022 (Arising out of Slp (Crl) No 4433 of 2022) Sheikh Abrar Sheikh Gaffar & Anr .... Versus State of Maharashtra ....R Order",
    "facts": "3 Crime No 488 of 2021 was registered against the appellants on 20 November 2021 at Police Station Paarva, District Yavatmal for offences punishable under Sections 188, 272, 273 and 328 read with Section 34 of the Indian Penal Code 18601 read with Sections 26 (2) (i), 27(2)(e), 30(2)(a) and 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. 4 The appellants were arrested on 20 November 2021. 5 The charge-sheet has been filed on 19 January 2022. 1 7 Bail has been granted to Accused Nos 3 and 4 in pursuance of an order dated 10 December 2021 of the Sessions Court at Yavatmal in Criminal Bail Application No 415 of 2021.",
    "arguments": "8 Counsel for the appellants has drawn the attention of the Court to the contents of paragraph 4 of the counter affidavit filed by the State before the High Court, in which it has been clarified that: 4. The present applicant No. 1 was driving the vehicle and the applicant No.2 was seating in the piloting vehicle i.e. Tata Sumo.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "8 Counsel for the appellants has drawn the attention of the Court to the contents of paragraph 4 of the counter affidavit filed by the State before the High Court, in which it has been clarified that: 4. The present applicant No. 1 was driving the vehicle and the applicant No.2 was seating in the piloting vehicle i.e. Tata Sumo.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
